§§ `On each shekel — a marginal scale`

-- "על כל שקל חדש" — ON EACH shekel of a band, that band's rate: a marginal scale, not a
-- slab (phrasebook 3.6). A band "from 301,201 to 560,280" is read as the slice of income
-- above 301,200 and up to 560,280, on a continuous amount; nothing in the slice rounds the
-- income or the tax to whole shekels (NOTES.md, fork F16).
GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `the bottom` IS A NUMBER
      `the top`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `above` `the bottom` `up to` `the top` MEANS
    max 0 (min `the income` `the top` MINUS `the bottom`)

GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `the bottom` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `beyond` `the bottom` MEANS
    max 0 (`the income` MINUS `the bottom`)

§§ `121(a) — the scale`

-- src:4351 | (1) על כל שקל חדש מ־301,200 השקלים החדשים הראשונים – 31%;
-- src:4352 | (2) על כל שקל חדש מ־301,201 שקלים חדשים עד 560,280 שקלים חדשים – 35%;
-- src:4353 | (3) על כל שקל חדש נוסף – 47%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)(1) (source line 4351)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate in section 121(a)(1)` MEANS 31%

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)(1)-(3) (source lines 4351-4353)
GIVEN `the taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`       IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(a) — the tax on` `the taxable income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
         `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `above` 0              `up to` `the top of (1)`)
    PLUS 35%                             TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `above` `the top of (1)` `up to` `the top of (2)`)
    PLUS 47%                             TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `beyond` `the top of (2)`)
    WHERE
        `the top of (1)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`
        `the top of (2)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 35% band`

§§ `121(b)(1) — the reduced rates`

-- src:4354 | (ב)(1) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א)(1) ובכפוף לאמור בפסקה (2), לגבי הכנסה חייבת בשנת המס מיגיעה אישית ולגבי הכנסה חייבת בשנת המס של יחיד שמלאו לו 60 שנים, יחולו שיעורים אלה:
-- src:4355 | (א) על כל שקל חדש מ־84,120 השקלים החדשים הראשונים – 10%;
-- src:4356 | (ב) על כל שקל חדש מ־84,121 שקלים חדשים עד 120,720 שקלים חדשים – 14%;
-- src:4357 | (ג) על כל שקל חדש מ־120,721 שקלים חדשים עד 228,000 שקלים חדשים – 20%;
-- src:4358 | (ד) על כל שקל חדש מ־228,001 שקלים חדשים עד 301,200 שקלים חדשים – 31%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)(a)-(d) (source lines 4355-4358)
GIVEN `the eligible income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`        IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the eligible income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
         10% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` 0         `up to` `top of (a)`)
    PLUS 14% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (a)` `up to` `top of (b)`)
    PLUS 20% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (b)` `up to` `top of (c)`)
    PLUS 31% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (c)` `up to` `top of (d)`)
    WHERE
        `top of (a)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 10% band`
        `top of (b)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 14% band`
        `top of (c)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 20% band`
        `top of (d)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band`

§§ `121(a) and (b)(1) together — "notwithstanding (a)(1)"`

-- (b)(1) opens "notwithstanding what is said in subsection (a)(1)": the reduced rates
-- displace (a)(1)'s 31% for the eligible income inside the first band, and nothing else.
-- So the tax is (a) on the whole income, less (a)(1)'s rate on the eligible part of the
-- first band, plus the reduced rates on that same part.
--
-- WHERE THE ELIGIBLE INCOME SITS (fork F1). s 121 does not say which shekels of the scale
-- the eligible income occupies when an individual also has other income on it. Taken: the
-- eligible income occupies the bottom of the scale, so the "first 84,120 shekels" of
-- (b)(1)(a) are the first 84,120 shekels of the eligible income. The other readings (the
-- eligible income on top; pro rata) are in NOTES.md. Where the Ordinance does settle the
-- order, it puts special-rate income at the highest step (ss 91(b)(1), 125C(b): src 3347,
-- 4530); those items are not on this scale at all here.
-- (0.3.0) RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): a switch, declined by default where the
-- placement changes the tax (below). Four readings, kept by name (nouns, `A reading of section
-- 121(b)(1) on where the eligible income sits on the scale`); the reasoning against reading (ii)
-- that 0.1.0 gave is corrected in NOTES.md, "Version 0.3.0".
--   at the bottom: the eligible income occupies the first shekels of the scale (0.1.0's reading);
--   the other income at the bottom: the eligible income sits above the other income, and the
--     reduced rate of each eligible shekel is the band its place on the scale falls in;
--   pro rata: each shekel of the scale is eligible in the proportion the eligible income bears to
--     all the income on the scale;
--   declined where the placement changes the tax (the default): the tax where the three agree, as
--     they do where all the income on the scale is eligible, or none of it, or where every
--     eligible shekel falls in the same reduced band under every placement (the independent
--     tester's F02); otherwise a refusal by name.
--
-- THE TWO TOPS OF THE 31% BAND. (a)(1) ends at "the first 301,200" and (b)(1)(d) at
-- "301,200"; the text prints the same figure twice and never says which governs if they
-- part. If a caller supplies ceilings in which they differ, the rule declines.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)-(b)(1) (source lines 4351-4358)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs` MEANS
    REFUSE "sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source lines 4354-4358); fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on where the eligible income sits on the scale`
`section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale` MEANS
    `declined where the placement changes the tax`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source lines 4354-4358); fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 121(b)(1) does not say which shekels of the scale the eligible income occupies when other income is on the scale too, and here the placement changes the tax` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 121(b)(1) does not say which shekels of the scale the eligible income occupies when other income is on the scale too, and here the placement changes the tax"

-- Each placement as arithmetic. R(x) is the reduced-rate tax on the first x shekels of the scale,
-- so the reduced-rate tax on the shekels from x to y is R(y) - R(x). In each, the tax is (a) on
-- the whole income, less (a)(1)'s rate on the eligible shekels inside the first band, plus the
-- reduced rates on those same shekels.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)-(b)(1) (source lines 4351-4358); fork F1
GIVEN `the taxable income`  IS A NUMBER
      `the eligible income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`        IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
      p                     IS A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on where the eligible income sits on the scale`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121 — the tax on` `the taxable income` `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` `the eligible income` `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings` `, placing the eligible income as` p MEANS
    IF   `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` EQUALS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`
    THEN CONSIDER p
         WHEN `the eligible income at the bottom of the scale` THEN `at the bottom`
         WHEN `the other income at the bottom of the scale`    THEN `on top`
         WHEN `the eligible income spread pro rata`            THEN `pro rata`
         WHEN `declined where the placement changes the tax`
           THEN IF   `at the bottom` EQUALS `on top` AND `at the bottom` EQUALS `pro rata`
                THEN `at the bottom`
                ELSE `section 121(b)(1) does not say which shekels of the scale the eligible income occupies when other income is on the scale too, and here the placement changes the tax`
    ELSE `sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs`
    WHERE
        -- The eligible income is at most the income itself.
        `the eligible`   MEANS min `the eligible income` `the taxable income`
        `the other`      MEANS `the taxable income` MINUS `the eligible`
        `the first band` MEANS min `the taxable income` (`the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`)
        `on the scale`   MEANS `s 121(a) — the tax on` `the taxable income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
        `at the bottom`  MEANS
                  `on the scale`
            MINUS `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES `the eligible at the bottom`
            PLUS  `s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the eligible at the bottom` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
        `the eligible at the bottom` MEANS min `the eligible` (`the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`)
        `on top`         MEANS
                  `on the scale`
            MINUS `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES `the eligible on top`
            PLUS  `s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` (`the other` PLUS `the eligible on top`) `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
            MINUS `s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the other` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
        `the eligible on top` MEANS max 0 (`the first band` MINUS `the other`)
        `pro rata`       MEANS
            IF   `the taxable income` EQUALS 0
            THEN `on the scale`
            ELSE       `on the scale`
                 MINUS `the share` TIMES (    `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES `the first band`
                                        MINUS `s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the first band` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`)
        `the share`      MEANS `the eligible` DIVIDED BY `the taxable income`

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)-(b)(1) (source lines 4351-4358); fork F1
GIVEN `the taxable income`  IS A NUMBER
      `the eligible income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`        IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121 — the tax on` `the taxable income` `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` `the eligible income` `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
    `s 121 — the tax on` `the taxable income` `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` `the eligible income` `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
        `, placing the eligible income as` `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`

§§ `The individual's income: what is on the scale, and what is eligible`

-- On the scale: every item of taxable income not charged at a rate of its own elsewhere.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a) (source line 4350); s 1 "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 117)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income charged at the rates in section 121 of` `the individual` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN i YIELD i's `charged at the rates in section 121`) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)))

-- "of an individual who has reached 60". Tested at the END of the tax year: an individual
-- whose 60th birthday falls on or before 31 December of the tax year (fork F2). Because the
-- tax year is a calendar year, that is the year of birth plus 60, and no leap-day case
-- arises.
-- (0.3.0) RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): fork F2 is a switch, declined by default where
-- the day of the test changes the tax. Four readings, kept by name (nouns, `A reading of section
-- 121(b)(1) on when the age of 60 is tested`):
--   60 by the end of the tax year: the test above (0.1.0's reading);
--   60 by the start of the tax year: the 60th birthday on or before 1 January of the tax year;
--   only the income derived after the 60th birthday: the age limb reaches only that income, which
--     is not an input of this model, so this reading declines where the age changes the tax;
--   declined where the day of the test changes the tax (the default).
-- The two tests differ only for an individual whose 60th birthday falls from 2 January to
-- 31 December of the tax year, and then only for income that is eligible by the age limb alone
-- (on the scale, not from personal exertion, books kept where required). The tax falls as the
-- eligible income grows, under every placement of fork F1, so where the two tests give the same
-- tax every reading does.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual` MEANS
    (DATE_YEAR (`the individual`'s `date of birth`) PLUS 60) AT MOST `the individual`'s `tax year`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2 (version 0.3.0)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aged 60 or more at the start of the tax year` `the individual` MEANS
        `the year of the 60th birthday` LESS THAN `the individual`'s `tax year`
    OR (    `the year of the 60th birthday` EQUALS `the individual`'s `tax year`
        AND DATE_MONTH (`the individual`'s `date of birth`) EQUALS 1
        AND DATE_DAY   (`the individual`'s `date of birth`) EQUALS 1)
    WHERE
        `the year of the 60th birthday` MEANS DATE_YEAR (`the individual`'s `date of birth`) PLUS 60

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on when the age of 60 is tested`
`section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested` MEANS
    `declined where the day of the test changes the tax`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 121(b)(1) does not say on what day of the tax year the individual must have reached 60, and here the day changes the tax` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 121(b)(1) does not say on what day of the tax year the individual must have reached 60, and here the day changes the tax"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2, the reading that only income derived after the 60th birthday is eligible by age
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this model does not have the income derived after the 60th birthday, which this reading of section 121(b)(1) needs here` MEANS
    REFUSE "this model does not have the income derived after the 60th birthday, which this reading of section 121(b)(1) needs here"

-- src:4359 | (2) השיעורים המופחתים הקבועים בפסקה (1) לא יחולו על הכנסה שחייבים לגביה בניהול פנקסי חשבונות ולא נוהלו לגביה פנקסים קבילים.
-- (0.3.0) Eligibility given whether the individual counts as having reached 60, which fork F2
-- decides; the forms without that argument keep their 0.2.0 names and decline where the two
-- tests of the age give different answers to what they ask.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359)
GIVEN `the item`           IS AN `An item of income`
      `has reached 60`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`eligible for the reduced rates` `the item` `, as income of an individual who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` `has reached 60` MEANS
            `the item`'s `charged at the rates in section 121`
    ...     "(b)(1)" ... (   `the item`'s `from personal exertion`
                          OR `has reached 60`)
    AND     "(b)(2)" ... NOT `the item`'s `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359); fork F2
GIVEN `the item`       IS AN `An item of income`
      `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`eligible for the reduced rates` `the item` `, as income of` `the individual` MEANS
    IF   `by the end` EQUALS `by the start`
    THEN `by the end`
    ELSE `section 121(b)(1) does not say on what day of the tax year the individual must have reached 60, and here the day changes the tax`
    WHERE
        `by the end`   MEANS `eligible for the reduced rates` `the item` `, as income of an individual who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual`)
        `by the start` MEANS `eligible for the reduced rates` `the item` `, as income of an individual who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more at the start of the tax year` `the individual`)

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359)
GIVEN `the individual`   IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
      `has reached 60`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` `, who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` `has reached 60` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN i YIELD `eligible for the reduced rates` i `, as income of an individual who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` `has reached 60`) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)))

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359); fork F2
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` MEANS
    IF   `by the end` EQUALS `by the start`
    THEN `by the end`
    ELSE `section 121(b)(1) does not say on what day of the tax year the individual must have reached 60, and here the day changes the tax`
    WHERE
        `by the end`   MEANS `the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` `, who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual`)
        `by the start` MEANS `the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` `, who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more at the start of the tax year` `the individual`)

§§ `Section 121 for an individual in a tax year`

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B`
`a problem with the items of income for section 121 of` `the individual` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount` LESS THAN 0) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)
    THEN JUST `an amount of income is negative`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The year is settled first, so that a year this model does not answer is declined in
-- return position rather than stored inside a RIGHT (phrasebook 11.8).
-- (0.3.0) The readings of forks F1 and F2 are arguments. The tax is settled before it is put in
-- a RIGHT, for the same reason: the test `the tax AT LEAST 0` (every tax here is, negative
-- amounts having been rejected) forces it, so a fork's refusal is in return position.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121 (source lines 4349-4359); forks F1, F2
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
      p                IS A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on where the eligible income sits on the scale`
      a                IS A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on when the age of 60 is tested`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`the tax under section 121 for` `the individual` `, placing the eligible income as` p `and testing the age of 60 as` a MEANS
    IF   `the text prints the section 121 ceilings for tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)
    THEN CONSIDER `a problem with the items of income for section 121 of` `the individual`
         WHEN JUST `the problem` THEN LEFT `the problem`
         WHEN NOTHING            THEN IF   `the tax` AT LEAST 0
                                      THEN RIGHT `the tax`
                                      ELSE RIGHT `the tax`
    ELSE `section 121 does not answer in this model for tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)
    WHERE
        `the income on the scale` MEANS `the taxable income charged at the rates in section 121 of` `the individual`
        `the tax, 60 by the end` MEANS
            `s 121 — the tax on` `the income on the scale`
                `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` (`the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` `, who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual`))
                `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings printed in section 121` `, placing the eligible income as` p
        `the tax, 60 by the start` MEANS
            `s 121 — the tax on` `the income on the scale`
                `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` (`the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` `, who, for section 121(b)(1), has reached 60:` (`aged 60 or more at the start of the tax year` `the individual`))
                `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings printed in section 121` `, placing the eligible income as` p
        `the tax` MEANS
            CONSIDER a
            WHEN `60 by the end of the tax year`   THEN `the tax, 60 by the end`
            WHEN `60 by the start of the tax year` THEN `the tax, 60 by the start`
            WHEN `only the income derived after the 60th birthday`
              THEN IF   `the tax, 60 by the end` EQUALS `the tax, 60 by the start`
                   THEN `the tax, 60 by the end`
                   ELSE `this model does not have the income derived after the 60th birthday, which this reading of section 121(b)(1) needs here`
            WHEN `declined where the day of the test changes the tax`
              THEN IF   `the tax, 60 by the end` EQUALS `the tax, 60 by the start`
                   THEN `the tax, 60 by the end`
                   ELSE `section 121(b)(1) does not say on what day of the tax year the individual must have reached 60, and here the day changes the tax`

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, by its old name, now at the readings the switches name.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121 (source lines 4349-4359); forks F1, F2
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`the tax under section 121 for` `the individual` MEANS
    `the tax under section 121 for` `the individual`
        `, placing the eligible income as` `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`
        `and testing the age of 60 as` `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested`

§§ `Editorial notes after section 121 — inert`

